.TH pipemixer.ini 5 "March 2026" "@VERSION@" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
pipemixer.ini \- configuration file for \fBpipemixer\fR(1)

.SH DESCRIPTION
The pipemixer.ini file configures the behavior and appearance of pipemixer.
.PP
pipemixer will look for a configuration file in the following locations:
.IP \(bu 4
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pipemixer/pipemixer.ini\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fB$HOME/.config/pipemixer/pipemixer.ini\fR, if XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.

.SH SECTION: main
General options.

.PP
.B volume-step
.RS 4
Volume change step as percentage (1 means 1%). Default: 1.
.RE
.PP
.B volume-min, volume-max
.RS 4
Max and min volume that can be set with pipemixer. Default: 0, 150.
.RE
.PP
.B wraparound
.RS 4
Whether scrolling through nodes will continue at the top after reaching the bottom and vice versa. Default: false.
.RE
.PP
.B mouse
.RS 4
Enable mouse input in the TUI. Default: true. Set to false to leave mouse
selection to the terminal.
.RE
.PP
.B tab-order
.RS 4
Order of tabs in the UI. A comma-separated string of tab names to be shown. Duplicate names are not allowed. Default: playback,recording,output-devices,input-devices,cards
.RE
.PP
.B default-tab
.RS 4
Specifies which tab will be active when pipemixer starts. Default: playback
.RE

.SH SECTION: binds
Configure keybindings. Format is action=key. Each action can be bound to multiple keys. Key can be specified in several ways:
.IP \(bu 4
All printable ASCII/Unicode characters.
.br
Example: tab-next=t
.IP \(bu 4
Special keys: up, down, left, right, enter, tab, backtab, space, backspace, escape.
.br
Example: tab-prev=backtab
.IP \(bu 4
Arbitrary keycodes with code:N, where N is a decimal number.
.br
Example: quit=code:185

.PP
.B focus-down, focus-up, focus-first, focus-last
.RS 4
Navigate list of items in the current tab.
.RE
.PP
.B volume-up, volume-down
.RS 4
Adjust volume.
.RE
.PP
.B volume-set-N
.RS 4
Set volume of selected item to N%.
.RE
.PP
.B tab-next, tab-prev
.RS 4
Cycle forward/backward through tabs.
.RE
.PP
.B tab-playback, tab-recording, tab-input-devices, tab-output-devices, tab-cards
.RS 4
Switch to specific tab.
.RE
.PP
.B tab-N
.RS 4
Switch to Nth tab (1-based).
.RE
.PP
.B mute-toggle, mute-enable, mute-disable
.RS 4
Set mute state for selected item.
.RE
.PP
.B channel-lock-toggle, channel-lock-enable, channel-lock-disable
.RS 4
Set channel lock for selected item.
.RE
.PP
.B set-default
.RS 4
Set focused source or sink as default.
.RE
.PP
.B select-route
.RS 4
Show device port selection menu.
.RE
.PP
.B select-target
.RS 4
Show the destination menu for a playback or recording stream.
.RE
.PP
.B toggle-routing
.RS 4
Open or close the live audio routing matrix.
.RE
.PP
.B manage-audio
.RS 4
Open the bus/send creation and managed audio path deletion menu.
.RE
.PP
.B manage-effects
.RS 4
Open effect creation or the focused effect's parameter editor.
.RE
.PP
.B manage-scenes
.RS 4
Open the scene save, load, delete and startup restoration selection menu.
.RE
.PP
.B manage-routing-rules
.RS 4
In the routing matrix, save an automatic rule for the selected output/input
ports. From the mixer, open the rule state, enable/disable and delete menu.
In the rule menu, h/l or Left/Right adjusts the focused rule's priority by 10.
.RE
.PP
.B save-routing-batch
.RS 4
In the routing matrix, save a glob rule for all compatible channels of the
selected source and target nodes. The default binding is A.
.RE
.PP
.B diagnostics
.RS 4
Open live per-channel peak/RMS/overload, CPU/memory, profiler and anomaly
monitoring for the focused node or routing source. Default i.
.RE
.PP
.B manage-recording
.RS 4
Open bounded audio cache creation, multitrack recording and export controls.
Completed capture sessions survive TUI exit. Default R.
.RE
.PP
.B manage-automation
.RS 4
Open automation, fades and MIDI/OSC management. The default key is o.
Complex rule definitions and external mappings are stored separately in
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pipemixer/automation.json (or ~/.config/pipemixer/automation.json).
.RE
.PP
.B manage-monitors
.RS 4
Open independent monitor creation/selection, normal mix/Solo editing,
listening source, enable/disable and deletion. Default M.
.RE
.PP
.B monitor-solo, monitor-listen, monitor-clear-solo
.RS 4
Toggle the focused source in the selected monitor's Solo list, listen to the
focused source, or clear all Solo and return to the stored listening choice.
Defaults S, L, U. Available in the mixer and routing matrix.
.RE
.PP
.B select-profile
.RS 4
Show profile selection menu.
.RE
.PP
.B confirm-selection, cancel-selection
.RS 4
Confirm or cancel selection when in menu.
.RE
.PP
.B quit
.RS 4
Exit application.
.RE
.PP
.B quit-or-cancel-selection
.RS 4
Behaves like cancel-selection if menu is active or as quit otherwise.
.RE
.PP
.B unbind
.RS 4
Unbind a key from any action.
.RE

.SH SECTION: interface
Configure various UI elements.

.PP
.B node-format, device-format
.RS 4
Strings controlling how information about nodes and devices is shown.
A format string can include property substitution in the following forms:

.IP \(bu 4
{prop} - Substitute the value of property if it exists, otherwise empty.
.IP \(bu 4
{prop?fmt} - Expand fmt if property exists, otherwise empty.
.IP \(bu 4
{prop!fmt} - Expand fmt if property does not exist, otherwise empty.
.IP \(bu 4
{prop?fmt1!fmt2} - Expand fmt1 if property exists, otherwise expand fmt2.
.IP \(bu 4
{prop?!fmt} - This is a shortcut idential to {prop?{prop}!fmt}

.PP
Nested substitutions are allowed.
Backslash can be used to escape characters {}?!, as well as itself.

.PP
You can obtain a list of properties for pipewire nodes with a command like:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
pw-dump | jq '.[] | select(.type == "PipeWire:Interface:Node") | .info.props'
.EE
.RE

.PP
Example of a format string that will print the value of node.description if it
is available and fall back to node.name otherwise, followed by a colon, a space,
and the value of media.name if media.name key exists:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
{node.description?!{node.name}}{media.name?: {media.name}}
.EE
.RE
.RE

.PP
.B bar-empty-char, bar-full-char
.RS 4
Characters for drawing volume bars.
.RE
.PP
.B routes-separator
.RS 4
String that separates routes on nodes that have them.
.RE
.PP
.B profiles-separator
.RS 4
String that separates profiles on devices.
.RE
.PP
.B border-left, border-right, border-top, border-bottom,
.br
.B border-top-left, border-top-right, border-bottom-left, border-bottom-right
.RS 4
Characters that make up border around each node.
.RE
.PP
.B volume-frame-top-left, volume-frame-top-right,
.br
.B volume-frame-bottom-left, volume-frame-bottom-right,
.br
.B volume-frame-center-left, volume-frame-center-right,
.br
.B volume-frame-mono-left, volume-frame-mono-right,
.br
.B volume-frame-focus
.RS 4
Characters that make up frame around per-channel volume bars.
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pipemixer (1)
